00:26:02,142 --> 00:26:08,142
Batman, a superhero created by Bob Kane and Bill Finger for comic books published by DC
Comics, has appeared in nearly every form of media, including film since the 1940s.

10
00:28:55,714 --> 00:29:01,714
Columbia Pictures supervised the first film adaptations with Batman (1943) and Batman
and Robin (1949), deviating significantly from the source material.

11
00:31:49,285 --> 00:31:55,285
20th Century Fox then released a theatrical spinoff of the American Broadcasting Company's (ABC)
live-action television series about the character in the 1960s, starring Adam West.

12
00:34:42,857 --> 00:34:48,857
After several years in limbo, Warner Bros.

13
00:37:36,428 --> 00:37:42,428
Pictures purchased the copyrights and developed a succession of Batman films in the late
twentieth century, two directed by Tim Burton and another pair by Joel Schumacher.

14
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Michael Keaton portrays Batman in the Burton films, while Val Kilmer and George
Clooney feature as the titular hero in the Schumacher films.

15
00:43:23,571 --> 00:43:29,571
Warner Bros.

16
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
spent the turn of the millennium in another protracted development period, leading to the production of a reboot trilogy
featuring Christian Bale as Batman: Batman Begins (2005), The Dark Knight (2008), and The Dark Knight Rises (2012).

17
00:49:10,714 --> 00:49:16,714
The creation of the DC Extended Universe (DCEU), a media franchise
bound by a shared universe, spawned additional works.

18
00:52:04,285 --> 00:52:10,285
Ben Affleck plays the character in the DCEU films, beginning with the Zack
Snyder-directed entry Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice (2016).

19
00:54:57,857 --> 00:55:03,857
Affleck, Keaton, and Clooney's Batmen have also
appeared in crossover films within the DCEU.

20
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
The Batman (2022) and The Brave and the Bold will revamp the established continuity of the live-action
films with new incarnations of Batman portrayed by Robert Pattinson and another actor.

21
01:00:45,000 --> 01:00:51,000
Joker (2019) features a depiction of the character as a civilian,
predating his transformation into a vigilante.

22
01:03:38,571 --> 01:03:44,571
Numerous actors voice Batman in animated film.

23
01:06:32,142 --> 01:06:38,142
The Batman films are generally successful and comprise one of the
highest-grossing franchises of all time, grossing over $6.8 billion globally.

24
01:09:25,714 --> 01:09:31,714
Critical opinion of films vary substantially.

25
01:12:19,285 --> 01:12:25,285
For example, The Dark Knight trilogy was critically acclaimed, whereas other films, such as
Batman & Robin (1997) and those of the DCEU, were not well reviewed in the media.

26
01:15:12,857 --> 01:15:18,857
Occasionally, Batman films attract Academy Award
recognition for acting and technical achievement.

27
01:18:06,428 --> 01:18:12,428
The tone is mind_bending and dark and thought_provoking.
